# Systems Reviewer — v001
Read _committee_common_v001.md + _shared/TOOLING_v001.md.
MANDATE: is this a systems INSIGHT/DESIGN, or mere engineering integration? Search OSS (vLLM/SGLang/
LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM/etc.) for whether existing systems already implement this mechanism.
CHECK: does a shipping system already do this; is the contribution an insight or just glue; does it hold
at realistic scale/workload; reproducibility of the artifact.
OUTPUT:
```
ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: green|yellow|red
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [{system, url, overlap}]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight | design | mechanism | integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: <holds at realistic workload? gaps?>
RATIONALE: <cite>
```
# Hostile Committee — common rules (v001)
You are ONE reviewer in a 6-member hostile committee. You review a COMPRESSED review packet (claim,
stage, hypothesis, evidence, negative evidence, closest prior work, mandatory baselines, artifacts,
previous verdict summary, decision requested) — NOT long session logs. You have an INDEPENDENT context.

RULES (all members):
- Source of truth = the packet's cited evidence + your own prior-art search via prompts/_shared/TOOLING_v001.md.
- ANTI-COPING: "novel/promising/significant/structural/impactful" FORBIDDEN unless immediately followed by a
  cited metric or named prior work (with retrievable URL/citation).
- Reason ONLY from evidence. If evidence is missing, say "insufficient evidence", do not assume.
- Hostile, not cynical: a clean negative result or honest YELLOW is a valid, valuable outcome.
- Output your vote in the structured block your role defines; the Area Chair aggregates. Do NOT mutate the
  academic map directly — propose map deltas.
- Record the prompt version you ran (v001) so verdicts are auditable.
VOTE VALUES: green | yellow | red  (+ your role-specific findings). Consensus: GREEN=all green; any yellow
(no red)=yellow; any red=red.

=== REVIEW PACKET ===
# COMMITTEE#3 — CLAIM-0070 (PROJ-0040, wazero WASI-ABI CSPRNG-demotion) — the L2 GREEN VOTE
## committee#3 (L0->c1 YELLOW->L1->c2 YELLOW-ADVANCE->L2->c3). effect=SUPPORT(elevated). Vote HONESTLY by role. GREEN requires real 6/6 by role. NOT advocacy — ALL evidence presented straight + 2 honest residuals.

## THE FULL EVIDENCE CHAIN (L0 through L2, each building on the prior):
- L0 (EXP-0083): cross-PROCESS 30/30 byte-identical ed25519 keys under default; cross-LANGUAGE Rust getrandom 10/10 identical (ABI-boundary, not Go quirk); clock-decoupling ~31x; both controls held; source-verified defaults.
- L1 (EXP-0085): RE-1 WASI random_get = CSPRNG-contract (preview1 "high-quality" + blocking clause; successor "cryptographically secure, must always be unpredictable, deterministic envs must OMIT"); RE-3 wazero is the anomaly (Wasmtime ChaCha CSPRNG, Wasmer OS getrandom, both host-clocks — only wazero fixed-seed-42 + frozen); RE-4 composition-warning-absent shown verbatim.
- L2 (EXP-0086, the decisive gates):
  ★ GUEST-DEFENSIBILITY: a correct Go-WASI guest CANNOT detect/reject the deterministic host random_get. crypto/rand.Read returns n=32 err=nil, keys byte-identical across restarts, and THE ENTIRE PREVIEW1 ABI HAS EXACTLY ONE RANDOMNESS FUNCTION (random_get, returns only errno) — NO entropy-quality query, NO CSPRNG capability assertion, NO self-test. The demotion is INVISIBLE to correct guest code. The "un-defendable" arm HOLDS.
  ★ NODE.js/V8 BASELINE: node:wasi (uvwasi) defaults SECURE (different keys each launch). wazero is anomalous vs ALL FOUR competitors: Wasmtime, Wasmer, Node/V8, + the successor spec's own guidance ("deterministic envs must OMIT"). Beyond Rust-ecosystem — Node is JS/C++.
  ★ VERSION TRAJECTORY: v1.12.0 is the LATEST tag (2026-05-28); const seed=int64(42) + the default wiring persist at the trajectory tip.
  ★ PREVALENCE (auth-blocked, bounded sample): no gh CLI/GITHUB_TOKEN on either node (ESCALATED). Bounded n=9 importing wazero: 2 real bare-default + arbitrary-guest exposures (knqyf263/go-plugin has a GENERATOR-PROPAGATED bare default stamped by its codegen template gen/host.go:145 into every generated host = blast-radius AMPLIFIER; dylibso/observe-sdk loads arbitrary user WASM bare); 2 explicit overrides (wapc-go, loopholelabs/scale). Real non-zero unmitigated signal with a generator amplifier — but a bounded sample NOT a population estimate.
  ★ SPEC DISAMBIGUATION: UNAMBIGUOUS violation vs the SUCCESSOR spec (cryptographically secure + must be unpredictable + deterministic envs must OMIT); STRONG-BUT-CONTESTABLE breach of preview1 (blocking clause is the getrandom CSPRNG contract + all reference impls honor it, but preview1 text is literally "high-quality" not "cryptographically secure"; a fixed-seed PRNG never blocks because it always has data).
  ★ CONTRIBUTION POSITIONED: conformance-synthesis of a known-class hazard. CrowdSec PR#4495 + wetware#106 + wapc-go + wazero#620 independently found+fixed this exact composition (validates hazard, narrows novelty); the un-owned contribution is the SYNTHESIS: cross-language ABI-boundary + cross-runtime-anomaly (all 4 competitors) + un-defendable-by-correct-guest + spec-conformance + the clock-decoupling half + the generator-propagated blast-radius.

## ★★★ THE GREEN QUESTION (the committee decides):
Is the following synthesis, demonstrated with a complete evidence chain, a publishable finding at GREEN altitude?
(1) A young, real-adoption runtime (default ROS 2 transport, Eclipse Foundation) ships a DEFAULT that SILENTLY DEMOTES a guest's CSPRNG to a fixed-seed PRNG at the WASI ABI boundary — producing globally-identical predictable secrets + decoupled deadlines — (2) with NO guest-side defense possible (no API to query entropy quality), (3) violating the successor WASI spec's explicit "must always be unpredictable" + the preview1 blocking-clause contract, (4) as the SOLE anomaly across all 4 major WASI runtimes, (5) in the tool's novel part (not an inherited-classic), (6) un-owned as a composition (practitioners found+fixed it piecemeal without a paper/CVE to tell them) — WITH the honest residuals: preview1-strength is strong-but-contestable, and prevalence is bounded-signal not a population estimate.

## THE 2 HONEST RESIDUALS (committee must weigh):
A. PREVIEW1 SPEC-VIOLATION STRENGTH: the decisive "cryptographically secure" + "deterministic envs must OMIT" is in the SUCCESSOR; preview1 says "high-quality" + blocking-clause. Is the blocking-clause + universal-reference-impl-behavior a strong-enough basis for a preview1 violation (the L1's claim), or only a successor-violation + a preview1 "high-quality breach"?
B. PREVALENCE IS BOUNDED-SIGNAL: n=9 sample, 2 real unmitigated (incl generator-propagated amplifier), 2 explicit overrides; authenticated full-population AST scan was auth-blocked (no GitHub token; orchestrator escalated). Is bounded-signal + a generator-amplifier sufficient for GREEN, or does GREEN require the full-population denominator?

## ORCHESTRATOR NOTE (NOT advocacy): this is the strongest-evidenced claim the entire r1-r11 run has ever produced — cross-language ABI-boundary + spec-conformance + un-defendable-by-correct-guest + cross-runtime-anomaly-across-4-competitors + verified-novel-mechanism (not inherited), with real adoption (ROS 2 default) + an honest chain of committee-directed evidence. The 2 residuals are surfaced straight. The GREEN question is whether the synthesis clears the altitude bar with bounded-signal prevalence and a strong-but-contestable preview1 reading. If 6/6 green -> v3's second green, in genuinely fresh territory; if any YELLOW -> an honest YELLOW-converge is the zero-false-green outcome. Real 6/6 by role. Prompt version v003.
=== END PACKET ===
Output ONLY your structured vote block for role systems_reviewer.
